<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia GDP(E) deflator fell 0.4 pct in Q3.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia GDP(E) deflator fell 0.4 pct in Q3.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's implicit price deflator for expenditure based GDP fell 0.4 percent in seasonally adjusted terms in the September quarter, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>The GDP(E) deflator in the year to September rose 1.3 percent.</p>
<p>Key deflator measures, as detailed in the national accounts, are tabled below.</p>
<p>Price Deflators	    Sept 96 June 96 Sept 95   Yr/Yr</p>
<p>Private Final Consump     +0.2    +0.3    +0.8	+1.4</p>
<p>Gross Nat'l Expenditure   -0.2    +0.4    +0.6	+0.6</p>
<p>GDP(E)			  -0.4    +0.9    +0.7	+1.3</p>
<p>Non-farm			-0.1    +1.0    +0.5	+1.9</p>
<p>Terms of trade		-0.2    +2.0    +1.0	+3.7</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
